cat > "/tmp/notebook_improvements_summary.md" << 'EOF'\
# Notebook Enhancements: Diagnostic Visualization\
\
## Overview\
Enhanced the `01_ProbabilisticFeatures.ipynb` notebook to provide comprehensive diagnostic plots across three categories of feature extraction outcomes, replacing the previous "failure-only" visualization approach.\
\
---\
\
## Changes Summary\
\
### 1. **Enhanced `plot_kde_diagnosis()` Function**\
\
#### Before:\
- Single plot function showing only collapsed topology cases\
- Minimal visual differentiation\
- Fixed title mentioning only "Topology Collapse"\
\
#### After:\
- **Status-aware visualization** with three modes: `"perfect"`, `"refined"`, `"failure"`\
- **Color-coded styling**:\
  - ‚ÉºÉ≥ **Perfect** (green background `#e8f5e9`, dark green peaks): Ideal first-attempt detection\
  - ‚É∫ÉπÔ∏ÉØ **Refined** (orange background `#fff3e0`, orange peaks): Adaptive bandwidth applied\
  - ‚ÉΩÉ¨ **Failure** (red background `#ffebee`, dark red peaks): Modal collapse persists\
- **Improved visual hierarchy**: Larger figure, better legend positioning, grid lines, denser plot\
- **Dynamic title prefix**: Emoji + status + batch/component info\
\
#### Key Improvements:\
```python\
# New parameters\
status : str  # "failure", "refined", or "perfect"\
\
# Color-coded backgrounds and markers based on status\
# Better visual hierarchy with line widths, marker sizes, zorder\
```\
\
---\
\
### 2. **Updated `get_adaptive_features()` Function**\
\
#### Before:\
- Returned only `(features, num_peaks_found)`\
- Plot control buried in calling code\
- No tracking of refinement iterations\
\
#### After:\
- **Returns triplet**: `(features, num_peaks_found, refinement_attempts)`\
  - `refinement_attempts = 0`: Perfect recognition on first try\
  - `refinement_attempts > 0`: Adaptive refinement applied\
  - Used to categorize outcomes\
- **Integrated plot control**: Parameters `plot_success`, `plot_refined`, `plot_failure`\
- **Cleaner status logic**: Determines category inside function, passes to plot\
\
#### Key Improvement:\
```python\
# New return value\
return features, num_peaks_found, refinement_attempts  # was just (features, num_peaks_found)\
\
# Automatic status determination and plotting\
if num_peaks_found < n_peaks_target:\
    status = "failure"\
elif refinement_attempts == 0:\
    status = "perfect"\
else:\
    status = "refined"\
```\
\
---\
\
### 3. **Redesigned Main Extraction Loop**\
\
#### Before:\
- Tracked only failures up to `MAX_DEBUG_PLOTS=5`\
- No visibility into success cases or refinement patterns\
- Limited statistics output\
\
#### After:\
- **Three tracking lists** (independent counters per category):\
  ```python\
  perfect_cases = []    # (batch_idx, component)\
  refined_cases = []    # (batch_idx, component, attempts)\
  failure_cases = []    # (batch_idx, component)\
  ```\
- **Target**: Up to 3 plots per category (configurable via `N_PLOTS_PER_CATEGORY`)\
- **Total visualization**: Up to 9 diagnostic plots (3 + 3 + 3)\
- **Summary statistics** printed at end:\
  ```\
  ‚ÉºÉ≥ Perfect (1st try):   N cases visualized (plots)\
  ‚É∫ÉπÔ∏ÉØ Refined (adaptive):  N cases visualized (plots)\
  ‚ÉΩÉ¨ Failures (collapsed): N cases visualized (plots)\
  ```\
\
#### Loop Logic:\
```python\
# For each component extraction:\
feats, num_peaks, attempts = get_adaptive_features(...,\
    plot_success=(len(perfect_cases) < N_PLOTS_PER_CATEGORY),\
    plot_refined=(len(refined_cases) < N_PLOTS_PER_CATEGORY),\
    plot_failure=(len(failure_cases) < N_PLOTS_PER_CATEGORY)\
)\
\
# Categorize and track\
if num_peaks >= 4:\
    if attempts == 0:\
        perfect_cases.append((i, 'I'))\
    else:\
        refined_cases.append((i, 'I', attempts))\
else:\
    failure_cases.append((i, 'I'))\
```\
\
---\
\
### 4. **New Markdown Section: "Feature Extraction Diagnostics"**\
\
Added comprehensive documentation (new cell before export) explaining:\
\
#### **Category 1: ‚ÉºÉ≥ Perfect Recognition**\
- What it represents: High-quality, low-noise scenarios\
- What to look for: Four clear peaks, minimal overlap, smooth structure\
- Interpretation: Constellation well-preserved\
\
#### **Category 2: ‚É∫ÉπÔ∏ÉØ Refined (Bandwidth Adaptation)**\
- What it represents: Moderate-to-high noise scenarios requiring statistical refinement\
- What to look for: Evidence of initial over-smoothing, final bandwidth smaller than default\
- Interpretation: Signal degradation but constellation distinguishable\
- **Key insight**: Bandwidth magnitude correlates with signal quality\
\
#### **Category 3: ‚ÉΩÉ¨ Failure (Topology Collapse)**\
- What it represents: Severe modal collapse from extreme noise/non-linearity\
- What to look for: < 4 peaks, fused distributions, high noise floor\
- Interpretation: OSNR < 5 dB or severe distortion\
- **Handling**: Zero-padded but flagged with warnings\
\
#### **Summary Statistics Section**\
- Explains how many plots were generated per category\
- Validates robustness across signal qualities\
\
---\
\
## Benefits\
\
### For Debugging:\
1. **Visual pattern recognition**: Easily spot which scenarios are problematic\
2. **Refinement insights**: See exactly how many iterations each case needed\
3. **Perfect baseline**: Compare good/bad cases side-by-side with same color scheme\
4. **Reproducibility**: Categorized cases can be re-examined later\
\
### For Documentation:\
1. **Comprehensive coverage**: All three outcomes documented with examples\
2. **Color-coded meanings**: Intuitive visual language (green=good, orange=caution, red=fail)\
3. **Pedagogical value**: Understanding feature extraction robustness at a glance\
\
### For Development:\
1. **Extensible**: Easy to adjust `N_PLOTS_PER_CATEGORY` or add new categories\
2. **Maintainable**: Clear separation of concerns (categorization, tracking, plotting)\
3. **Scalable**: Works regardless of dataset size\
\
---\
\
## Visual Examples\
\
### Perfect Case\
```\
Background: Green (#e8f5e9)\
Title: ‚ÉºÉ≥ PERFECT: Batch 42 Component I\
Peaks: Dark green X markers (4 clear peaks)\
Key: All peaks found on first KDE attempt\
```\
\
### Refined Case\
```\
Background: Orange (#fff3e0)\
Title: ‚É∫ÉπÔ∏ÉØ REFINED: Batch 103 Component Q\
Peaks: Dark orange X markers (4 peaks after bandwidth reduction)\
Key: Bandwidth reduced 0.6√É∑ once to resolve modal collapse\
```\
\
### Failure Case\
```\
Background: Red (#ffebee)\
Title: ‚ÉΩÉ¨ FAILURE: Batch 7 Component I\
Peaks: Dark red X markers (only 2-3 peaks despite 3 retries)\
Key: Severe modal collapse; constellation fundamentally degraded\
```\
\
---\
\
## Implementation Notes\
\
1. **Backward Compatible**: Existing code that processes features is unaffected\
2. **No Data Changes**: Feature output `X_features` remains identical\
3. **Optional Visualization**: Plots only generated if data is present; processing continues otherwise\
4. **Memory Efficient**: Tracking lists contain only indices, not data\
\
---\
\
## Testing Recommendation\
\
After running the updated notebook:\
1. Check that exactly 3 plots appear per category (or fewer if dataset doesn't have enough cases)\
2. Verify color-coding matches documentation (green, orange, red)\
3. Compare successful vs. refined vs. failed bandwidth values in titles\
4. Confirm summary statistics at end match the plotted cases\
\
EOF
